ision he also did something else  when the advice we had of those set-to  with him even on the question of islands  where we agreed pretty much that  something should be done about violence  on television he did an editorial of his  own on the network and saying that if  you agree with me there's so much  violence on television right your  Congressman and tell him to do something  about it well that now we're raising the  First Amendment question I believe  something should be done about it but by  an outraged public I don't believe that  Congress should do anything because the  Constitution says the Congress shall  make no law and and so I could not  explain  due to Turner that when you're talking  about Congress should do something about  it you've lost me because you've lost me  on First Amendment grounds and so we had  a little argument about that too a  couple of things some of them big some  small  you taught me where the word MIG came  from you're the MIG aircraft where did  it come from well this all happened  because because I was covered I was  recently back to Havana where it al 40  years ago I was there when Deputy Prime  Minister Anastas Mikoyan of the Soviet  Union came on the first important  official Soviet visit to Castro and I  recall this to him only recently when I  was Havana again and as you remember  that the question was whether you were  going to get MIG airplanes from the  Soviet Union he's right and you remember  you were talking to the right man  because McKeon's brother was a designer  of the made the MIG it mi is Michael Yan  and the G is gravich those were the two  designers of the big you lost two-thirds  of your stomach  a large part of my professional life was  clouded by the fact that I had a  duodenal ulcer and also was not just a  physical problem what it was was that it  would interfere with my making  appointments with my social life with my  planning trips because I never knew when  it was going to act up and so I was  always 