t clever aggressive fellow fellow  Nikita Khrushchev had different things  in mind he wanted to bring the Soviet  Union somehow into the modern age while  still protecting communism and because  he was very outgoing would turn up at  diplomatic receptions all the time and  so it was possible to see him almost  every three or four days and check with  him how what was going on there was he  finally agreed to do a television  interview he appeared on CBS's Face the  Nation from his office in the Kremlin  the first ever interview with a Soviet  leader on television even on Soviet  television and wherever he went I would  go I was sort of a Soviet version of a  White House correspondent and was he  regarded as very amusing  sometimes referring to me as his Sputnik  because I was in orbit around him all  the time and then we have time there was  one very funny story with his job and  that was not one that was that was this  1956 was a very tense time Hungary was  going up in flames the war being fought  over Suez in the Middle East and whose  chef came back from an unusually long  vacation in October amid rumors that the  Soviet Central Committee was going to  make and take some drastic action or  some kind on either on Hungary or the  Middle East's and troops to Egypt or  something like that we couldn't even  find out on the conditions they were  there and as the Central Committee was  meeting or was going  to me and so because of my about a  special relationship with whose job I  undertook to find out at a reception I  went up to him when we talked about ten  minutes about his vacation he had had  Tito with him they hunted in the Crimea  and all arrests finally I said mr.  Khrushchev you think I could go down to  the Crimea must be beautiful there now  and paralysis of course you can notion  to somebody just  reynad but I have a problem maybe you  can even help me with a problem my  capitalist bosses back in New York CBS  had told me that I can't leave Moscow  because 